"links":367,"meta":368,"navigation":369,"path":65,"seo":370,"stem":66,"__hash__":371},"docs\u002F01.apps\u002F05.persistence\u002F01.overview.md",{"type":231,"value":232,"toc":358},"minimark",[233,237,242,282,286,289,317,321,324],[234,235,236],"p",{},"Kinotic provides a declarative persistence layer. You define entities with TypeScript decorators, and Kinotic generates fully typed CRUD services automatically, including full-text search, pagination, and more.",[238,239,241],"h2",{"id":240},"key-features","Key Features",[243,244,245,253,264,270,276],"ul",{},[246,247,248,252],"li",{},[249,250,251],"strong",{},"Automatic CRUD generation"," - Define an entity class and get a complete service with create, read, update, delete, search, and count operations",[246,254,255,258,259,263],{},[249,256,257],{},"Full-text search"," - Mark fields with ",[260,261,262],"code",{},"@Text"," to enable full-text search out of the box",[246,265,266,269],{},[249,267,268],{},"Schema evolution"," - Use versioned migration scripts to evolve your data schema safely over time",[246,271,272,275],{},[249,273,274],{},"Multi-tenancy"," - Built-in tenant isolation at the data layer with shared index support",[246,277,278,281],{},[249,279,280],{},"Named queries"," - Define custom query methods with a SQL-like syntax",[238,283,285],{"id":284},"workflow","Workflow",[234,287,288],{},"The typical workflow for working with Kinotic persistence is:",[290,291,292,301,311],"ol",{},[246,293,294,297,298],{},[249,295,296],{},"Define your entity"," - Create a TypeScript class with decorators from ",[260,299,300],{},"@kinotic-ai\u002Fpersistence",[246,302,303,306,307,310],{},[249,304,305],{},"Sync to server"," - Run ",[260,308,309],{},"kinotic sync"," to push your entity definitions to the Kinotic server and generate typed service classes",[246,312,313,316],{},[249,314,315],{},"Use in your app"," - Import and use the generated services to perform data operations",[238,318,320],{"id":319},"packages","Packages",[234,322,323],{},"Two packages work together to provide the persistence layer:",[243,325,326,346],{},[246,327,328,332,333,336,337,336,340,336,343,345],{},[249,329,330],{},[260,331,300],{}," - Provides entity decorators (",[260,334,335],{},"@Entity",", ",[260,338,339],{},"@AutoGeneratedId",[260,341,342],{},"@NotNull",[260,344,262],{},", etc.), entity service interfaces, and the persistence plugin",[246,347,348,353,354,357],{},[249,349,350],{},[260,351,352],{},"@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore"," - Provides the connection layer (",[260,355,356],{},"Kinotic.connect()","), pagination types, and core utilities shared across all Kinotic packages",{"title":359,"searchDepth":360,"depth":360,"links":361},"",2,[362,363,364],{"id":240,"depth":360,"text":241},{"id":284,"depth":360,"text":285},{"id":319,"depth":360,"text":320},"Kinotic's persistence layer provides declarative data management with automatic CRUD service generation from TypeScript entity definitions.","md",null,{},true,{"title":25,"description":365},"sgwciN4UxMGGqqWq9TLwhEfjY-sUhA5nQbcCAXm8m_s",[373,375],{"title":55,"path":56,"stem":57,"description":374,"children":-1},"Real-time data streaming between services and clients.",{"title":68,"path":69,"stem":70,"description":376,"children":-1},"How to define entities using TypeScript decorators for Kinotic's persistence layer.",1790398954112]